# AWS EC2 Incident Postmortem — CPU Spike (Simulated)

**Author:** Piyush Awasthi
**Date:** 10 July 2026
**Environment:** AWS Free Tier — EC2 (Amazon Linux), Apache (httpd), CloudWatch
**Severity:** SEV-3 — single instance, lab environment, no customer impact
**Status:** Resolved

---

## 1. Summary

A CPU exhaustion event was simulated on a single EC2 instance (`web01`) using the `stress` utility to validate CloudWatch's CPU monitoring and alarm configuration. The exercise also surfaced a real gap in the initial alarm configuration — the alarm's evaluation period required 3 consecutive breaching datapoints over 15 minutes, which an intermittent (non-sustained) load did not satisfy even though CPU briefly exceeded the 70% threshold. [CONFIRM: state here whether the final run triggered "In alarm" or whether you adjusted the alarm's datapoints-to-alarm setting to 1-of-1 to validate the mechanism.]

